The package whiteoutlib provides CMake targets:

    find_package(WhiteoutLib CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE WhiteoutLib::whiteout_lib)

`whiteout_lib` links every module the port was built with. A consumer that
needs less links the modules themselves, and names them as components so a
missing one fails at configure time:

    find_package(WhiteoutLib CONFIG REQUIRED COMPONENTS wem_convert casc)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE
        WhiteoutLib::whiteout_wem_convert
        WhiteoutLib::whiteout_casc)

Modules and their features (all four are default features):

    whiteout_core           always
    whiteout_textures       whiteoutlib[textures]
    whiteout_models         whiteoutlib[models]
    whiteout_wem            whiteoutlib[models]
    whiteout_wem_convert    whiteoutlib[wem-convert]
    whiteout_wem_edit       whiteoutlib[wem-edit]

Each storage component corresponds to the matching vcpkg feature
(`whiteoutlib[casc]`, `whiteoutlib[mpq]`, `whiteoutlib[database]`).
